{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0024","billNumberShort":"H.B. 24","billNumberLong":"HB0024S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0825","shortTitle":"Criminal Penalty Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"WILCORD","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Wilcox, Ryan D.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MUSSECR","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Musselman, Calvin R.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses criminal penalties.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>reduces the criminal offense of operating a vehicle at a speed greater than 20 miles per hour in a school zone from a class C misdemeanor to an infraction if the person is operating the vehicle from 21 miles per hour to 29 miles per hour;<hr><ltbullet>merges the criminal offenses of:<hr><ltbullet1>operating a motor vehicle without an owner's or operator's security; and<hr><ltbullet1>failing to carry evidence of owner's or operator's security to be carried when operating a motor vehicle;<hr><ltbullet>reduces the penalty for the criminal offense of careless driving from a class C misdemeanor to an infraction; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Shad Larson","fiscalAnalyst":"Noah Matthew Hansen","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"DPSUNDWUUL","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-04 17:54:41.277","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-04 17:54:41.277","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2